# The client bucket now delegates memory/pid controllers and joins the
# delegated supervisor before testing. Its platform-enforcement waivers
# are no longer necessary; all client native fixtures must run.

# The ordinary fast bucket does not install bwrap. The jailed Linux lane
# installs it and runs this exact tools test without a skip declaration.
declared|linux|SKIP git worktree: helper has no filesystem enforcement|The ordinary tools bucket cannot enforce the outside write; the jailed Linux lane runs the real Git worktree approval fixture with bubblewrap.

# The language-server manager's `gopls` fixture drives a real `gopls`
# through the jail on a two-package Go module. It is feature-detected: a
# runner without `gopls` (or without `go`, which `gopls` shells out to)
# prints this line and passes. The `gleam lsp` fixture beside it needs only
# the toolchain every runner has, so the manager's door, its jail and its
# probe are still exercised against a real server without this waiver.
declared|linux|SKIP lsp manager gopls: gopls or go is not installed|The ordinary runner installs no gopls; the gleam lsp fixture in the same file runs the whole door against a real jailed server, and a host with gopls on PATH or at ~/go/bin runs this one.
